node_modules

# Project-customized agent definitions (subagent system prompts). Kept machine-local by
# choice, not because they're generic — some override built-ins (Explore, Plan) and some
# are wholly project-specific (cross-repo-synthesis, doc-sync-auditor, wq-ticket-writer,
# engine-mechanics-researcher), several of which reference the private uma-tools-plans repo.
# Anything tracked that depends on one of these existing (e.g. .claude/skills/project-review/
# SKILL.md's cross-repo-synthesis call) must degrade gracefully when it's absent, since a
# fresh clone won't have this directory.
.claude/agents/

# Worktrees for parallel per-ticket work (CLAUDE.md's Branching & PRs section: "Worktrees
# live under .claude/worktrees/"). Machine-local scratch checkouts, never meant to be
# tracked. Wasn't ignored at all until this line: a worktree under here nests a full
# checkout of the uma-skill-tools submodule, and being merely untracked (not ignored)
# was enough for uma-tools-plans/scripts/check-citations.py's marker walk to pick it up
# as a second copy of every engine ANCHOR, reporting each as "defined in both repos" and
# blocking that repo's own pre-commit hook for as long as the worktree existed -- see
# uma-tools-plans PIPE-39 for the matching fix on that script's own ignore-detection
# (it separately failed to treat a whole ignored *directory* the same as an ignored file,
# so this line alone wasn't sufficient there either, but is still correct and necessary
# defense-in-depth: worktrees categorically don't belong in this repo's history).
.claude/worktrees/

# .claude/settings.json is tracked: shared project config (the PIPE-49
# submodule cwd-drift guard hooks). Personal machine-local preferences --
# permission allowlists (which Bash/MCP calls skip the approval prompt),
# personal hooks -- live in settings.local.json instead, which stays
# untracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Bulk import of personal Claude Code session state (agent defs, session
# memory/feedback notes with real incident writeups and session UUIDs, and
# copies of the .claude/skills/ files) from an "agy import" -- machine-local
# by nature, never meant to be tracked. Was accidentally committed (see
# d3b0521); this stops it from being tracked going forward. `.claude/skills/
# handoff` and `.claude/skills/claude-handoff` symlink into `.agents/skills/`
# and will dangle on a fresh clone as a result -- known, not fixed here.
.agents/

# Local alias to CLAUDE.md for tools that discover AGENTS.md. The symlink is
# intentionally checkout-local; CLAUDE.md is the tracked source of truth.
AGENTS.md

# Local-only planning notes (backlog ideas, not part of the shipped repo).
# No trailing slash: plans/ is a symlink to a sibling repo (../uma-tools-plans) on this
# machine, and a trailing-slash pattern only matches real directories, not symlinks.
plans

# Extracted game client DB used locally to regenerate skill/uma/course data.
# Large binary, never meant to be committed - see docs/data-pipeline.md.
# Glob (not just the literal master.mdb) so a differently-named copy -- e.g.
# master_jp.mdb, the JP client alongside the unsuffixed Global master.mdb -- is
# caught too. Naming convention: JP-specific files get an underscore server
# suffix (master_jp.mdb, meta_jp, dat_jp/); Global stays completely unsuffixed
# (master.mdb, meta, dat/) -- there is no "_global" variant. See
# docs/master-mdb-schema.md.
*.mdb

# esbuild output for every app with a build.mjs. deploy.yml rebuilds these on
# every push and Pages is configured to serve that CI artifact (build_type:
# workflow) — see docs/deployment.md. Do NOT add a blanket */bundle.js here:
# build-planner's source doesn't compile against the current uma-skill-tools
# layout (see docs/apps.md), so its stale bundle.js/bundle.2.js stay committed
# on purpose. It is the only remaining app without a build.mjs.
/umalator/bundle.js
/umalator/bundle.css
/umalator/simulator.worker.js
/umalator-global/bundle.js
/umalator-global/bundle.css
/umalator-global/simulator.worker.js
/skill-visualizer-global/bundle.js
/skill-visualizer-global/bundle.css
/skill-visualizer/bundle.js
/skill-visualizer/bundle.css
/courseimages/bundle.js
/courseimages/bundle.css
/rougelike/bundle.js
/rougelike/bundle.css
/umadle/bundle.js
/umadle/bundle.css

# Playwright smoke-test artifacts (scripts/smoke.mjs) -- screenshots + report, never committed
/scripts/smoke-artifacts/

# Encrypted game client asset-manifest DB (meta) and its decrypted-plaintext sibling
# (scripts/decrypt-meta-db.mjs's output) -- same story as *.mdb above, large binaries
# never meant to be committed, see docs/data-pipeline.md. "meta_*" catches the JP copy
# (meta_jp) the way *.mdb does for master DBs; the game ships the unsuffixed Global
# file as literally "meta" with no extension, so it isn't caught by *.mdb and needs
# its own pattern. "meta-*" (dash) is kept alongside "meta_*" (underscore) so a local
# file not yet renamed to the current convention doesn't silently become un-ignored
# (PIPE-17 review, 2026-08-28).
meta
meta_*
meta-*
*.decrypted

# Local asset-extraction working directories (scripts/download-game-assets.mjs,
# scripts/extract-assets.py) -- downloaded/decrypted Unity asset bundles and their
# unpacked contents. Large, regeneratable, never meant to be committed. Glob covers
# a per-server copy (dat_jp/, a future dat_en/) the way meta_* does above.
/dat/
/dat_*/
/need_unpack/

# Python venv for scripts/extract-assets.py (UnityPy) -- see docs/data-pipeline.md.
/scripts/.venv/

# Scratch notes for in-progress work (e.g. project-review findings not yet applied) --
# working notes only, never meant to be committed or shipped.
/tmp/

# Working directory for files that might be useful for future work (downloaded game data,
# decoded saves, HAR captures, etc.) plus temp files while working -- never meant to be
# committed or shipped.
/scratchpad/
